This mutation makes `bank_t2` ignore safe-altar tiles that hold a camp or an unseen camp spawn. Right now `closest(SAFE_RING)` can return a camp tile, so `bank_blocked` never sees the "every altar-adjacent tile is blocked" case it is meant to catch. With camp tiles removed, `bank_t2` goes invalid in that case and `bank_blocked` can fire, while `bank_goal` still gets a walkable target whenever one exists.

```python
@gene("m14b", "nearest tile next to a safe altar that holds no camp (camp tiles are not walk goals here)", parents=["m14"])
def bank_t2() -> Tile:
    return closest(SAFE_RING - camp_block())
```

The mutation edits `step_gain` only. It keeps the field-downhill rule but refuses a one-tile step onto a tile within 2 of a visible enemy champion, so the bot doesn't walk one step closer into a fight it can't win. `move_value` and `act_value` are left unchanged, since their ranking already prefers larger gains.

```python
@gene("w6", "how much closer a step onto t brings me to GOAL (0: no walk this turn); turn-start field and blocks; a 1-tile gain onto a tile within 2 of an enemy champion is refused", parents=["w6"])
def step_gain(t: Tile) -> Num:
    if not OPEN or t in BLOCK:
        return 0
    g = at(FIELD, here()) - at(FIELD, t)
    if g <= 1:
        if g == 1 and count(1 for x in enemies() if x.is_champion and dist(x.pos, t) <= 2) > 0:
            return 0
    return g
```

This mutation changes only `adj_altar` (m2). It now prefers an altar next to us that no enemy lock blocks, and falls back to any adjacent altar. That way `r_prefight` and `r_pass` are less likely to bank into a locked altar, where the tribute would hit the lock instead of scoring.

```python
@gene("m2b", "an altar next to us, preferring one not enemy-locked", parents=["m2"])
def adj_altar() -> Tile:
    open_alt = first_tile(altars() & near(here(), 1) - locked_altars())
    if valid(open_alt):
        return open_alt
    return first_tile(altars() & near(here(), 1))
```

This mutation changes `blocked_now` so the walking field also avoids tiles next to enemy occupancy, except camp tiles and my own tile. The idea is that retreat and bank walks stop stepping adjacent to enemy champions. I have not run it, so the effect on camp walking is untested.

```python
@gene('B104b', 'tiles I cannot step onto: terrain, altars, enemy spawn, units, unseen camp spawns, plus tiles next to enemy units (camp tiles excluded)', parents=['B104a'])
def blocked_now() -> Tiles:
    base = TERRAIN | ally_tiles() | enemy_tiles() | camp_block()
    near_foe = ring(enemy_tiles(), 1) - camp_block()
    return (base | near_foe) - near(here(), 0)
```

This mutation narrows the unseen-camp blocking in `blocked_now`. Unseen camp spawns beyond 10 tiles no longer block the walk field. Those spawns are usually far from the short walks the rules make, and treating them as walls can force detours or cut off routes to altars. I kept the seen-camp and terrain blocks, plus the removal of the tile I stand on. I have not run this against the arena, so the effect is untested.

```python
@gene('B104b', 'tiles I cannot step onto now: terrain, altars, enemy spawn, units, seen camps, and unseen camp spawns within 10 tiles', parents=['B104a'])
def blocked_now() -> Tiles:
