```

The edit makes `taken()` also exclude tiles next to visible enemy champions, so `closest` won't pick a goal beside an enemy. `walk_open` uses `taken()` too, so it will treat such goals as unwalkable. I haven't run it.

```python
@gene("w12b", "tiles held by something other than a camp, plus tiles next to visible enemy champions (never a goal)", parents=["w12"])
def taken() -> Tiles:
    T = blocked() - camp_block()
    for u in enemies():
        if u.is_champion:
            T = T | near(u.pos, 1)
    return T
```

